Prefer Linux terminal font fallbacks over Apple emoji/system glyphs.

cosmic-text's macOS fallback list jumps from Apple UI/terminal fonts directly to
Apple Color Emoji. In cosmic-term that means terminal glyphs can be resolved from
a different provider on macOS than on Linux; zellij box-drawing borders can come
from Menlo/Apple fonts instead of the Noto/DejaVu terminal fallback chain used on
Linux, and text-presentation symbols can fall through to Apple Color Emoji.

Put the same common Linux fallback families first on macOS, then keep the native
Apple fallbacks. This keeps terminal glyphs such as U+2502 (BOX DRAWINGS LIGHT
VERTICAL) and U+23FA (BLACK CIRCLE FOR RECORD, Claude Code's message/tool
bullet) in the installed Noto/DejaVu monochrome fonts before Apple-specific
fallbacks are considered.

The U+23FA glyph lives in Noto Sans Symbols 2, whose real family name contains a
space ("Noto Sans Symbols 2"). fontdb matches family names exactly, while
cosmic-text's unix.rs only includes the unspaced "Noto Sans Symbols2"; keep that
unix fix as well. The macOS Braille script fallback is also aligned with Unix's
FreeMono fallback so spinner glyphs stay monospaced.

These symbol fonts cover technical/text symbols but not pictographic emoji, so
real emoji (e.g. U+1F534) still resolve to the color emoji font.

--- a/src/font/fallback/macos.rs
+++ b/src/font/fallback/macos.rs
@@ -31,6 +31,19 @@
     &[
+        // Match the Linux common fallback order first so terminal glyphs (box
+        // drawing, powerline-adjacent symbols, text-presentation symbols) use
+        // the same installed Noto/DejaVu providers on macOS before falling back
+        // to Apple UI fonts or Apple Color Emoji.
+        "Noto Sans",
+        "DejaVu Sans",
+        "FreeSans",
+        "Noto Sans Mono",
+        "DejaVu Sans Mono",
+        "FreeMono",
+        "Noto Sans Symbols",
+        "Noto Sans Symbols 2",
+        "Noto Sans Symbols2",
         ".SF NS",
         "Menlo",
         "Apple Color Emoji",
         "Geneva",
         "Arial Unicode MS",
@@ -65,6 +78,9 @@
         Script::Adlam => &["Noto Sans Adlam"],
         Script::Arabic => &["Geeza Pro"],
         Script::Armenian => &["Noto Sans Armenian"],
+        // Match Unix: Braille glyphs are common terminal spinner characters,
+        // and FreeMono avoids proportional fallback alignment changes.
+        Script::Braille => &["FreeMono"],
         Script::Bengali => &["Bangla Sangam MN"],
         Script::Buhid => &["Noto Sans Buhid"],
         Script::Canadian_Aboriginal => &["Euphemia UCAS"],
--- a/src/font/fallback/unix.rs
+++ b/src/font/fallback/unix.rs
@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@
         /* Symbols fallbacks */
         "Noto Sans Symbols",
         "Noto Sans Symbols2",
+        // The Noto Sans Symbols 2 family name actually contains a space; the
+        // unspaced spelling above doesn't match it in fontdb. U+23FA (Claude
+        // Code's bullet) lives here, so without this it falls through to the
+        // color emoji font and renders as a filled block.
+        "Noto Sans Symbols 2",
         /* Emoji fallbacks*/
         "Noto Color Emoji",
         //TODO: Add CJK script here for doublewides?
